{"id": "EUVD-2026-108680", "enisaUuid": "c6fe0169-24fe-3e8e-9781-e029305095a5", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/gma500: return errors from Oaktrail HDMI I2C reads\n\nxfer_read() waits for the HDMI I2C transaction to reach\nI2C_TRANSACTION_DONE, but it ignores both timeout and signal returns from\nwait_for_completion_interruptible_timeout().  If the interrupt never\nadvances the transaction state, the loop can wait forever.\n\nReturn -ETIMEDOUT when the completion wait expires, propagate interrupted\nwaits, and make the I2C master_xfer callback return the first transfer\nerror instead of reporting a successful message count.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T11:37:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T11:37:43", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/09a950950e7e4e74e021e60941c8e816ef1b4f71", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/898d209157fe2a245f7d9fe28c5921037d8b5033", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/15c6d7f7127a53b7312232178ecf03e5850161d2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8add43887cca1fe11a0ded62199ce726901d3f20", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f85e8224bd4e1a0939cbfe13a6220fbddf61127c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c268df0653ab07bafc3d191e74ea097e3d9b9e69", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9b5ce5c496efd20c1c662cedba88465d39ec1f93"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98886"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "01f4d87e-baf5-3124-92b2-c91c94c0aa71", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "15013f2a-f11e-3d2c-b3ad-fd098b4e2e01", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0 <5.15.222"}, {"id": "1df90969-a466-31f9-b93b-e7c888a35923", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <9b5ce5c496efd20c1c662cedba88465d39ec1f93"}, {"id": "2623a460-ae13-3e82-9156-2283759a745c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendo